   "text": "Runtime and persistence rules",
   "originalText": "Runtime and persistence rules",
   "fontSize": 24,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": false
  },
  {
   "id": "e209",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1520,
   "y": 716,
   "width": 2320,
   "height": 225,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#212529",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 435025238,
   "version": 2,
   "versionNonce": 2023881840,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "• Checkpointer (S1) saves AgentState after every node, keyed by thread_id. Crash or restart with the same thread_id resumes at the last finished node.\n• N1 runs on a fresh invoke or a new task. Crash-resume with None skips N1; a new task on an existing thread gets a new run_id.\n• Human gates (H1–H4) call interrupt(response_schema=…): state is persisted, the process can exit, and Command(resume={Interrupt.id: value}) continues it hours or days later.\n• Approval queue: RunController owns astream; pending is keyed by Interrupt.id; the queue is a projection of state.interrupts; the TUI shows one request at a time.\n• Parallelism: R4 returns one Send(...) per ready step; subagents share the parent run/checkpoint; N7 joins results through step_results. Two subagents can interrupt in the same superstep.\n• Limits: recursion_limit + per-subagent iteration cap + token / cost / time budgets checked in N8 (R6).\n• Context discipline: raw tool output goes to S3, state keeps references only; N9 compacts when R7 sees > 70% of OLLAMA_NUM_CTX.\n• Model: local Ollama via ChatOllama; MODEL_NAME from .env; no API key; cost $0.00 (local).\n• Safety: shell and file tools run in an isolated workspace; risky tools need H3 approval; secrets never enter prompts.\n• Observability: trace every node, router decision, tool call and approval; stream events (v2, subgraphs=True) to the CLI / TUI.",
   "originalText": "• Checkpointer (S1) saves AgentState after every node, keyed by thread_id. Crash or restart with the same thread_id resumes at the last finished node.\n• N1 runs on a fresh invoke or a new task. Crash-resume with None skips N1; a new task on an existing thread gets a new run_id.\n• Human gates (H1–H4) call interrupt(response_schema=…): state is persisted, the process can exit, and Command(resume={Interrupt.id: value}) continues it hours or days later.\n• Approval queue: RunController owns astream; pending is keyed by Interrupt.id; the queue is a projection of state.interrupts; the TUI shows one request at a time.\n• Parallelism: R4 returns one Send(...) per ready step; subagents share the parent run/checkpoint; N7 joins results through step_results. Two subagents can interrupt in the same superstep.\n• Limits: recursion_limit + per-subagent iteration cap + token / cost / time budgets checked in N8 (R6).\n• Context discipline: raw tool output goes to S3, state keeps references only; N9 compacts when R7 sees > 70% of OLLAMA_NUM_CTX.\n• Model: local Ollama via ChatOllama; MODEL_NAME from .env; no API key; cost $0.00 (local).\n• Safety: shell and file tools run in an isolated workspace; risky tools need H3 approval; secrets never enter prompts.\n• Observability: trace every node, router decision, tool call and approval; stream events (v2, subgraphs=True) to the CLI / TUI.",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": false
  },
