   "versionNonce": 1083807327,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Rules",
   "originalText": "Rules",
   "fontSize": 20,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": false
  },
  {
   "id": "e512",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2760,
   "y": 6184,
   "width": 1040,
   "height": 700,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#212529",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 411512151,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 12379493,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "• One thread per session. Send subagents share the parent run; never create a thread per subagent.\n\n• Use Interrupt.id, not request_id, as the resume key. request_id is UI/audit only.\n\n• Resume one at a time; LangGraph re-interrupts the remaining tasks. Batching is optional.\n\n• One astream per thread; only RunController resumes. The TUI never calls the graph.\n\n• Approvals arrive per superstep. While paused, no new interrupt can appear.\n\n• Emit requests from __interrupt__ / state.interrupts, never before interrupt().\n\n• No side effects before interrupt(); a resumed node restarts from its top.\n\n• The queue is a projection of state.interrupts; rehydrate on restart.\n\n• Dedupe events by interrupt_id; a resume replays node/text events.\n\n• Keep payloads compact; full diff/command lives in S3 (artifact_id).\n\n• H1/H2/H3/H4 share this inbox, status model and audit table.\n\n• Cancel = reject/abort all pending; mark them CANCELLED.",
   "originalText": "• One thread per session. Send subagents share the parent run; never create a thread per subagent.\n\n• Use Interrupt.id, not request_id, as the resume key. request_id is UI/audit only.\n\n• Resume one at a time; LangGraph re-interrupts the remaining tasks. Batching is optional.\n\n• One astream per thread; only RunController resumes. The TUI never calls the graph.\n\n• Approvals arrive per superstep. While paused, no new interrupt can appear.\n\n• Emit requests from __interrupt__ / state.interrupts, never before interrupt().\n\n• No side effects before interrupt(); a resumed node restarts from its top.\n\n• The queue is a projection of state.interrupts; rehydrate on restart.\n\n• Dedupe events by interrupt_id; a resume replays node/text events.\n\n• Keep payloads compact; full diff/command lives in S3 (artifact_id).\n\n• H1/H2/H3/H4 share this inbox, status model and audit table.\n\n• Cancel = reject/abort all pending; mark them CANCELLED.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": false
  }
 ],
